stupid that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:47:05-07:00","id":1069295,"title":"","content":"And? What's bad with that? Technically, 1E Skinchangers already <i>are </i>'sorta Wolf-Blooded', by the way 2E <b>Werewolf</b> defines Wolf-Blooded...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-28-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T17:26:28-07:00","id":1070398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1069286-2e-changing-breeds-and-skinchangers-relations?p=1069295#post1069295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And? What's bad with that? Technically, 1E Skinchangers already <i>are </i>'sorta Wolf-Blooded', by the way 2E <b>Werewolf</b> defines Wolf-Blooded...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most skinchangers have no-relation to werewolves, and most Wolf-Blooded cannot change shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-29-2017, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T17:42:48-07:00","id":1070402,"title":"","content":"I always got the impression that Changing Breeds was to Chronicles of Darkness as the Philips CDI games were to Zelda. Yeah, technically they happened, but we all kind of pretend they were just a bad dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:17:11-07:00","id":1070436,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: Skinchangers was a book. It had skinthieves (reproduced via merit in Dark Eras) but it also included a wide variety of Werewolf antagonists of different stripes. Asking for relationships between Changing Breeds and Skinchangers is impossible, because some of the skinchangers were fox spirit possessing bodies, or crazy snake hybrids, each with their own origin story.<br /> <br /> Skinthieves, on the other hand, are to Werewolves as psychic vampires are to Kindred. Lots of relationships, intertwined stories, but a clear differntiation.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for relationships? I personally would make everything revolve around Werewolves (or another major gameline) than I would between two minor things. Mortal/psychics, vampires, werewolves, witches (I basically houseruled mage until it was basically a new game), promethean and changeling. Take a pick of one of those six, and that's what the relationship webs grow from. <br /> <br /> For me, when I start charting out everything that a Changing Breed could concievably fill, I already have something else in place I prefer. Snake shifters? Vampires pretty much cover the serpetine better than even a snake shifter, imho. Something like the tengu or other bird-men? We have not only spirits but strix that do that well. Fox and cats end up as changeling Kitsune and Cait Sith types that happen to be popular. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-29-2017, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],